# Work product — keep the reproducible layer, ignore bulk data & rendered blobs.
#
# The team's institutional memory is its *text*: queries (.sql), write-ups
# (FINDINGS.md / SPEC.md / DESIGN.md / MODEL_CARD.md), scripts (.py), specs, and
# inventory READMEs — these stay in git so every number is reproducible and the
# history is auditable (CLAUDE.md principle 3). What's ignored below is the
# large or potentially confidential output: raw extracts, datasets, and rendered
# decks/workbooks/PDFs that can be regenerated from the tracked code.
#
# To preserve a specific output anyway, force-add it: `git add -f path/to/file`.

# Bulk data & extracts (regenerate from the pipeline / query)
*.csv
*.tsv
*.parquet
*.feather
*.avro
*.orc
*.jsonl
*.ndjson
*.sqlite
*.db
*.duckdb

# Rendered deliverables & BI binaries (reproducible from analysis + SOURCES.md)
*.pptx
*.docx
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.pdf
*.twbx
*.pbix
*.pbit
*.zip

# Tableau workbooks: a .twb is plain XML and diffs cleanly, so it IS tracked —
# same principle as PBIP below. Its build.py is the source and the .twb the
# output, but reviewing what changed in a workbook is the point of the module.
# The packaged .twbx and the .hyper extract are binaries and stay ignored.

# Power BI Projects (PBIP): the .pbip / .pbir / .tmdl / .json text IS tracked —
# it's the reproducible layer, same as .sql and .md. Only the binary cache and
# per-user state are ignored (these two lines match what Power BI Desktop
# generates itself when you save as a project).
**/.pbi/cache.abf
**/.pbi/localSettings.json

# Secrets / environment files
.env
.env.*
*.env
!.env.example
secrets.*
*.key
*.pem
credentials.json
service-account*.json

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/

# Jupyter
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.gstack/

# Pre-setup snapshots written by scripts/setup_backup.py. Local safety net for
# undoing /setup-team — restore with `--restore <timestamp>`, never committed.
.setup-backup/

# Tableau runtime schema cache - extracted from a local Tableau install.
# Proprietary Tableau content; never commit it (see
# .claude/skills/tableau/scripts/extract_runtime_schema.py).
.claude/skills/tableau/schemas/.runtime-cache/

# Tableau extracts and packaged workbooks are generated binaries.
# The .twb, build.py and the SQL are the reproducible layer and ARE tracked.
*.hyper
*.twbx

# Hyper API writes a log beside the working directory.
hyperd.log
